    "html": "<p><strong>Tehran, Iran –</strong>Strikes around the strategic Strait of Hormuz have picked up again as mediated efforts to end the US-Israel war on Iran remain deadlocked.</p><p>The Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) Navy said on Saturday night that an unnamed crude oil supertanker hit a naval mine and suffered a major fire while using an unauthorised route in the waterway with navigation systems turned off. In a statement, it warned of a similar fate for any oil tanker that “wishes to ignore the security and rules” of the strait, through which one-fifth of the world’s oil and gas passes in peacetime.</p><figure class=\"md-image\"><img src=\"https://dev.data.muslimsday.com/appdata/blog/media/2026/10/d67d191a-1665-491d-b062-eb9a73a37f15.jpg\" srcset=\"https://dev.data.muslimsday.com/appdata/blog/media/2026/10/d67d191a-1665-491d-b062-eb9a73a37f15-640.webp 640w, https://dev.data.muslimsday.com/appdata/blog/media/2026/10/d67d191a-1665-491d-b062-eb9a73a37f15-1024.webp 1024w, https://dev.data.muslimsday.com/appdata/blog/media/2026/10/d67d191a-1665-491d-b062-eb9a73a37f15.jpg 1280w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" width=\"1280\" height=\"963\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"></figure><aside class=\"md-callout md-callout--info\" role=\"note\"><p>Warning! be careful! Ho ha hah</p></aside><h2 id=\"recommended-stories\">Recommended Stories</h2><p>list of 3 items</p><ul><li>list 1 of 3<a href=\"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/9/is-trump-signalling-a-return-to-war-with-iran-after-the-midterms\"><strong>Is Trump signalling a return to war with Iran after the midterms?</strong></a></li><li>list 2 of 3<a href=\"https://www.aljazeera.com/news-analysis/2026/10/10/anachronism-rubios-civilisational-rhetoric-prompts-pushback-from-iran\"><strong>‘Anachronism’: Rubio’s civilisational rhetoric prompts pushback from Iran</strong></a></li><li>list 3 of 3<a href=\"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/11/us-forces-disable-ship-attempting-to-run-iran-blockade-in-gulf-of-oman\"><strong>US forces disable ship ‘attempting to run’ Iran blockade in Gulf of Oman</strong></a></li></ul><p>end of list</p><p>On Sunday, a senior Iranian army official told state television that the country’s forces remain prepared for both defensive and offensive operations, more than seven months since the United States and Israel started the war by attacking Iran on February 28.</p><blockquote><p>We have struck blows against enemy vessels. If anything else happens against Iran, we will strike them again</p></blockquote><p>said Habibollah Sayyari, chief of staff and joint coordinator of the army.</p><div class=\"md-ad\" data-ad=\"custom\"><script async src=\"https://adserve.kahf.to/tag.js\" data-placement=\"pl_cebbd311f0a444b4\" data-formats=\"banner\"></script>\n<div id=\"ad-pl_cebbd311f0a444b4\"></div></div><p>His comments came after the United Kingdom Maritime Trade Operations (UKMTO) reported several incidents of<a href=\"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/9/28/iran-touts-hormuz-attacks-as-oil-flows-increase-despite-tensions\"><u>military action or warnings against vessels</u></a>in the Strait of Hormuz and Gulf of Oman over the past day. It said ship masters in the vicinity of Ras al-Khaimah, in the United Arab Emirates (UAE), had been directed via radio broadcast overnight to move from their anchorages. And on Sunday afternoon, UKMTO reported ⁠an unidentified projectile had struck a tanker ⁠heading outbound through the Strait of ⁠Hormuz.</p>",
